<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2026/8/eng@/~part_I__cl_3> <https://schema.org/name> "In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires—"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2026/8/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2026/8/eng@/~part_I__cl_3> <https://schema.org/text> "“technical means” includes the use of any device, equipment, software, program, computer code, network or other technological means; “content data” means any computer data, other than subscriber information or traffic data, relating to the substance of the data transferred by a computer system, including images, text messages, voice messages, audio recordings and video recordings; “computer data” means any representation of facts, information or concepts in a form suitable for processing in a computer system which includes a program suitable to cause a computer system to perform a function, including content data, traffic data and subscriber information; “traffic data” means any computer data relating to a communication by means of a computer system, generated by a computer system that forms a part in the chain of communication, indicating the communication’s origin, destination, route, time, date, size, duration or type of underlying service; “property” means an asset of every kind, whether corporeal or incorporeal, movable or immovable property, tangible or intangible, including virtual asset, digital currency and legal documents or instruments evidencing title to, or interest in, such asset; “Committee” means the Committee on Combating Cybercrimes established under section 4; “Chief Executive” means the Chief Executive of the National Cyber Security Agency; “communications” means any communication, whether between persons and persons, things and things, or persons and things, in the form of sound, data, text, visual images, signals or any other form or any combination of those forms; “subscriber information” means any information held by a service provider, relating to subscribers of its services, other than traffic data or content data, and which can be established by—"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2026/8/eng@> .
